@TKCollective Fully aligned. That is why PR #3682 establishes the explicit claim ceiling:

`VALID_x402ev != CORRECT_DELIVERY != PROVEN_EXECUTION != AUTHORIZED_TRANSITION`

The receipt format only binds settlement to delivered bytes and counterparty signature; it does not mandate hardware enclaves or dictate dispute logic. Downstream evaluation and whether evidence authorizes a state transition remain strictly within the relying party's declared policy.
